PLAIN ENGLISH SUMMARY (not legally binding)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  FREE:   Run Meridian locally on your own machine for any purpose —
          personal, commercial, research, internal tooling. Any team
          size. Connecting to a shared hosted database (Neon, Supabase,
          etc.) is explicitly free. Self-hosting internally is free
          provided you don't publish how-to guides or deployment tooling
          for others to do the same.

  PAID:   Hosting Meridian or a functionally equivalent product as a
          service you offer to others. Building a competing coordination
          platform. Publishing deployment tooling whose primary purpose
          is enabling third parties to operate Meridian commercially.

  NEVER:  The above during the Protection Period without a commercial
          license from us.

  LATER:  After 6 years from first public release of each version, that
          version automatically becomes MIT — no strings attached.

